            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical manifestations of ischemic heart disease in the subacute period of myocardial infarction and post-infarct cardiosclerosis depending on the status of coronary arteries].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-40</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Multifactor discriminant analysis was used on a computer to examine 100 patients with myocardial infarction in the subacute period (at week 4 of the disease onset) and 76 in the postinfarction period (at months 2-120 of postinfarction). A complex of clinical and coronary signs was defined, which differentiated patients with subacute myocardial infarction and postinfarct cardiosclerosis, as well as those with postinfarct stable and progressive angina pectoris.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
